Nuevo Universal Keyboard:

The Dvorak typewriter keyboard letter scheme is designed for writing using two-hands. It is apposite for writing any language that uses the Latin, Cyrillic or Greek script.

Note: The US(English) Post-Mechanical keyboard is hardwired to use the native QWERTY driver. Users should not install the Microsoft ISO driver,

Note: Linux OS users of the US(English) Post-Mechanical will use the native US-QWERTY driver.

The US English ISO driver was written to facilitate developing European language drivers (the locations of the '[ ]' and '- =' key sets are swapped).

The Post-Mechanical Dvorak 2025 keymap has 48 character keys. This makes it compatible with ISO keyboards.

I have created and tested Windows drivers for several European languages. Linux drivers will be developed next, Apple is not my wheelhouse.

Ronald Earl Walker
